{"id":"code-roman","title":"Integer to Roman numeral","category":"code","difficulty":2,"prompt":"Write a Python function `to_roman(n: int) -> str` that converts an integer from 1 to 3999 to a Roman numeral in standard subtractive notation (4 is IV, 9 is IX, 40 is XL, and so on).","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"to_roman","tests":["assert to_roman(1) == \"I\"","assert to_roman(4) == \"IV\"","assert to_roman(9) == \"IX\"","assert to_roman(14) == \"XIV\"","assert to_roman(40) == \"XL\"","assert to_roman(90) == \"XC\"","assert to_roman(400) == \"CD\"","assert to_roman(1994) == \"MCMXCIV\"","assert to_roman(2024) == \"MMXXIV\"","assert to_roman(3999) == \"MMMCMXCIX\""]},"reference":"```python\ndef to_roman(n: int) -> str:\n    table = [\n        (1000, \"M\"), (900, \"CM\"), (500, \"D\"), (400, \"CD\"), (100, \"C\"), (90, \"XC\"),\n        (50, \"L\"), (40, \"XL\"), (10, \"X\"), (9, \"IX\"), (5, \"V\"), (4, \"IV\"), (1, \"I\"),\n    ]\n    out = []\n    for value, symbol in table:\n        while n >= value:\n            out.append(symbol)\n            n -= value\n    return \"\".join(out)\n```","answers":["```python\ndef to_roman(n: int) -> str:\n    table = [\n        (1000, \"M\"), (900, \"CM\"), (500, \"D\"), (400, \"CD\"), (100, \"C\"), (90, \"XC\"),\n        (50, \"L\"), (40, \"XL\"), (10, \"X\"), (9, \"IX\"), (5, \"V\"), (4, \"IV\"), (1, \"I\"),\n    ]\n    out = []\n    for value, symbol in table:\n        while n >= value:\n            out.append(symbol)\n            n -= value\n    return \"\".join(out)\n```","```python\ndef to_roman(n: int) -> str:\n    table = [(1000, \"M\"), (500, \"D\"), (100, \"C\"), (50, \"L\"), (10, \"X\"), (5, \"V\"), (1, \"I\")]\n    out = []\n    for value, symbol in table:\n       